Both reject '//evil.com' but accept '/\evil.com'. The WHATWG URL parser normalises a backslash to a forward slash in the path of a special scheme, so the value parses as a protocol-relative URL: node -e 'console.log(new URL("/\\evil.com","https://app.propdesk.africa").href)' prints https://evil.com/ - and the server answers 307 Location: https://evil.com/.

