Two defects: (1) x-forwarded-for is the FIRST value of a client-supplied header, and most proxies prepend rather than replace it, so the first hop is attacker-controlled; the app should read a platform-trusted header (x-vercel-forwarded-for / cf-connecting-ip). (2) when MPESA_ALLOWED_CALLBACK_IPS is unset the function returns true for everyone unless MPESA_ENV === 'production' - and MPESA_ENV defaults to 'sandbox' (lib/mpesa/daraja.ts:47).

